## 🧪 How I Verified It

- 65 primary sources fetched and read; each retained with its URL.
- Source conflicts resolved in writing rather than silently — e.g. Anthropic's ISO 42001 appears on the certifications article but *not* on the regional-compliance page, which lists 27017/27018/CSA STAR instead. The discrepancy is disclosed in the app.
- Scoring logic tested programmatically: all 24 provider-criterion cells checked for score range, valid evidence flag, non-trivial justification and at least one source reference; every source reference validated to resolve within the 65-item list; rankings recomputed under all six presets plus six single-criterion dominance tests to confirm the model is actually sensitive to weighting.
- Refused to publish either the 30-day or 90-day Vertex retention figure. Guessing correctly and guessing are the same act.

---

## ⚠️ Limits of the Model

- Six criteria, linear weighting, no interaction effects — in reality residency and retention constrain each other.
- Cost, latency, model quality and ecosystem are deliberately excluded. This scores **governability**, not value.
- First-party surfaces only. Claude via Bedrock or Vertex scores very differently, because the processor changes.
- Compliance posture moves monthly. Everything here is a snapshot dated 4 Sep 2026 — re-verify before any real approval decision. Not legal advice.

